-- title:
--   Round six: normalization of the CrudeAssembly hypotheses to a parameter record
-- statement:
--   Let $a_b, a_c \ge 0$ be the savings of S. Jain's round-six bit and complex networks, i.e. assume the moment bounds
--
--   $$\mu_{1-a_b}(h_{\mathrm{bit}}; 529) < 148225616, \qquad \mu_{1-a_c}(h_{\mathbb C}; 576) < 207387136,$$
--
--   where $\mu_\tau(h; m) = \sum_{(w,n_w) \in h} n_w\,(w/m)^{\tau}$ is the moment of the child-width histograms $h_{\mathrm{bit}} = $ `Jain.bitR6`, $h_{\mathbb C} = $ `Jain.cxR6` (from `Def_IntMul_KappaJainData`). Assume further the crude-assembly constraints `CrudeAssembly` $(a_b, a_c, \beta = 1/1000, \varepsilon, x, C_1, \kappa, 576, s_c)$ of the κ framework, with $s_c$ the rank sum of $h_{\mathbb C}$.
--
--   Then there is a parameter record $P = (\tau, \sigma, \varepsilon', \lambda', x', C_1')$ with $P$ satisfying all the constraints `Prm.Ok` (in particular $1/2 \le \varepsilon' < 1$, $0 < \tau, \sigma \le 1$, natural $x' \ge 1$), with $\kappa < \mathrm{gap}(P)$ (the minimum of the five cost margins), with the two moment bounds holding at the exponents $\tau = P.\tau$ and $\sigma = P.\sigma$, and with the depth-guard condition
--
--   $$2 + 576 \log s_c \le C_1'.$$
--
--   This is the first step of the round-six argument: all later statements are parametrized by such a record $P$, and the reduction to $\varepsilon \ge 1/2$ means only one cost regime has to be treated.
--
--   In Lean:
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.r6_normalize (ab ac ε x C₁ κ : ℝ) (hab : 0 ≤ ab) (hac : 0 ≤ ac)
--       (hbit : histMoment Jain.bitR6 529 (1 - ab) < 148225616)
--       (hcx : histMoment Jain.cxR6 576 (1 - ac) < 207387136)
--       (hasm : CrudeAssembly ab ac (1 / 1000) ε x C₁ κ 576 (histRankSum Jain.cxR6)) :
--       ∃ P : Prm, P.Ok ∧ κ < P.gap ∧ histMoment Jain.bitR6 529 P.τ < 148225616 ∧
--         histMoment Jain.cxR6 576 P.σ < 207387136 ∧
--         2 + 576 * Real.log (histRankSum Jain.cxR6) ≤ P.C1
--   ```
--
